s four I had an older  brother who played been playing since I  was eight I wasn't the best when I was a  kid but  I kept at it I started playing hockey at  13 years old I was born and raised in  the island soon as I came to the states  one of the first thing I've asked my dad  was when can we go hit the ice I  remember it was only one girl per team  and my dad didn't want me playing out  with the guy so he put me in net and he  thought that was safer  my parents they wanted to put me in  figure skating and I said absolutely not  I want to hit some boys like my brother  so I got into hockey and I've been  playing ever since  hockey's my escape from life being able  to get away from my personal life  problems or just having a bad day just  being on the ice just it's an amazing  feeling being able to play with people  who have the same love for the game  and try to get my breath I honestly just  go to the place of why why I'm here who  am I doing it for the one thing we want  to keep going is is the growth of this  organization and the nation and Puerto  Rico hockey within itself finding this  team has been something that I will  always be so grateful for being able to  be in a team that we all share the same  struggles but in so many different  stories it's really comforting to be the  best teammate I think about  representation and growing the game I  think about the young boys and girls  that are seeing us for the first time  and understanding that wow I can do that  all I want to do is give these players  of color and opportunity to play the  game that we all love love to see that  the stadium rink is full of supporters I  am very acutely aware there are those of  us who represent a more vast and diverse  community in hockey so I see this  tournament as a way of amplifying our  history and pushing our narrative into  the Forefront for the future of this  sport  [Applause]

